error[B0707]: `net.out(pay.example.com)` is performed by more than one definition, so a stub cannot answer from the call
  --> t.beck:187:5
    |
187 |     stub net.out(pay.example.com):
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `charge`, `refund` both perform it
    |
  = note: a stub that matches on arguments has to know whose arguments they are; a stub that is a plain value does not, and still works here
  = help: give the one you mean its own atom — a second host or a second store — or stub a value instead of a block
